WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.955
Settle in bed or another safe resting place.

2
00:00:05.655 --> 00:00:10.000
A quiet mind does not have to be empty.

3
00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:19.760
This practice changes how you relate to bedtime thinking without promising sleep or requiring thoughts to stop.

4
00:00:25.382 --> 00:00:27.222
Feel the body supported.

5
00:00:28.922 --> 00:00:34.376
Notice one broad contact area and one sound in the room.

6
00:00:36.076 --> 00:00:40.806
Let the present environment be available alongside thought.

7
00:00:52.050 --> 00:00:54.130
Observe the next thought that appears.

8
00:00:55.830 --> 00:01:00.605
Do not search for one and do not finish it deliberately.

9
00:01:02.305 --> 00:01:07.045
Notice that a thought can arrive by itself.

10
00:01:18.288 --> 00:01:30.823
Give it a light label: planning, remembering, rehearsing, worrying, imagining, or simply thinking.

11
00:01:32.523 --> 00:01:39.383
Let the label describe the activity rather than the truth of the content.

12
00:01:52.499 --> 00:01:56.859
Return to the weight of the body for one breath.

13
00:01:58.559 --> 00:02:02.774
Thought is present, and support is present.

14
00:02:04.474 --> 00:02:06.474
Neither needs to remove the other.

15
00:02:19.591 --> 00:02:25.491
When another thought appears, imagine placing its subject on a page for tomorrow.

16
00:02:27.191 --> 00:02:33.691
You do not need to picture the page clearly or trust that every detail will be remembered.

17
00:02:46.808 --> 00:02:50.308
Use the phrase: noted for later.

18
00:02:52.008 --> 00:02:56.568
Then let attention come back to the bed beneath you.

19
00:03:09.685 --> 00:03:11.445
Some thoughts may repeat.

20
00:03:13.145 --> 00:03:18.130
Recognize repetition as the mind checking the same door again.

21
00:03:19.830 --> 00:03:27.610
You can answer with the same brief phrase rather than a new argument.

22
00:03:42.601 --> 00:03:47.941
Notice the gap after one thought fades and before another becomes clear.

23
00:03:49.641 --> 00:03:55.821
The gap may be a second, a fraction of a second, or not easy to find.

24
00:03:57.521 --> 00:03:58.801
Do not hold it open.

25
00:04:11.918 --> 00:04:16.578
Let sounds be more interesting than thoughts for a while.

26
00:04:18.278 --> 00:04:23.243
Hear near and far sounds without naming their source.

27
00:04:24.943 --> 00:04:26.983
Let each one end on its own.

28
00:04:43.847 --> 00:04:45.847
Return to the body.

29
00:04:47.547 --> 00:04:51.367
Feel the forehead, jaw, and hands.

30
00:04:53.067 --> 00:05:03.197
If these areas are working around a thought, let them reduce effort by one small degree.

31
00:05:16.314 --> 00:05:22.914
If a practical concern truly needs action tonight, acknowledge that choice.

32
00:05:24.614 --> 00:05:27.014
You may pause the practice and act.

33
00:05:28.714 --> 00:05:35.149
Quieting the mind does not mean ignoring safety or responsibility.

34
00:05:48.266 --> 00:05:55.921
If no action is needed now, try: nothing to solve in this breath.

35
00:05:57.621 --> 00:06:03.406
Feel one inhale and one exhale without using them to force calm.

36
00:06:18.397 --> 00:06:23.412
Imagine thoughts as messages passing across a dim screen.

37
00:06:25.112 --> 00:06:30.522
You can notice that a message exists without opening every thread.

38
00:06:45.512 --> 00:06:53.492
If imagery is unhelpful, return to simple language: thought, then contact.

39
00:06:55.192 --> 00:06:58.302
Thought, then sound.

40
00:07:00.002 --> 00:07:02.042
Move between them without judgment.

41
00:07:18.907 --> 00:07:26.902
Notice whether the mind is asking, am I asleep yet, is this working, how long has it been.

42
00:07:28.602 --> 00:07:30.322
Label checking.

43
00:07:32.022 --> 00:07:34.022
Let the question remain unanswered.

44
00:07:49.012 --> 00:07:52.172
Feel the whole resting body.

45
00:07:53.872 --> 00:08:00.052
Let awareness be broad enough that no single thought occupies the entire field.

46
00:08:16.917 --> 00:08:20.197
Now release labels for several moments.

47
00:08:21.897 --> 00:08:31.557
Thoughts may come with words, images, fragments, or unfinished shapes.

48
00:08:33.257 --> 00:08:35.657
Allow them to be incomplete.

49
00:08:58.143 --> 00:09:04.283
If you find yourself following a story, return at the moment you notice.

50
00:09:05.983 --> 00:09:12.323
There is no penalty for having followed it and no need to retrace the path.

51
00:09:27.314 --> 00:09:32.559
Let the next three thoughts pass without response if you can.

52
00:09:34.259 --> 00:09:39.069
If one captures attention, begin again with the next one.

53
00:10:01.555 --> 00:10:06.405
Notice that the mind may be active while the body still rests.

54
00:10:08.105 --> 00:10:13.460
Rest does not have to wait for complete mental silence.

55
00:10:30.324 --> 00:10:46.869
Let attention settle on the darkest or quietest part of present experience: closed eyes, distant sound, the bed's steady contact, or the pause after an exhale.

56
00:11:05.608 --> 00:11:06.528
Stay lightly.

57
00:11:08.228 --> 00:11:12.743
If sleepiness comes, stop following the instructions.

58
00:11:14.443 --> 00:11:23.293
If wakefulness remains, let this be a period of resting rather than a test of sleep.

59
00:11:43.905 --> 00:11:48.875
There is nothing to empty and nothing to finish here.

60
00:11:50.575 --> 00:12:00.000
Let thought become one small kind of movement inside a larger, supported night.
